Quick note — you wrote “SSN is XXX-XX-3456 (last four: 1234).” Which is the correct last-four digits (3456 or 1234)? I’ll assume you mean you only want the last 4 visible; confirm and I’ll tailor any wording or redaction example.

General guidance (best practices)
- Never send a full SSN over plain email or in a filename/subject unless absolutely required and you know the recipient’s secure handling procedures.
- If the form only needs the last four digits, redact the first five digits and show only the last four (e.g., XXX-XX-1234 or ***-**-1234).
- If the recipient requires the full SSN, ask them for a secure method (secure upload portal, encrypted email, or password-protected file) before sending.
- Use true redaction (removal), not just covering text with white/black boxes that leave the underlying text recoverable by copy/OCR.

How to redact safely
1. Paper-first option (recommended if you have the paper original):
   - Permanently black out the first five digits with an opaque permanent marker or approved redaction tape, then scan the document.
   - Inspect the scanned image to confirm the digits are not readable or recoverable.

2. Digital redaction (recommended tools/methods):
